  "title": "Answer: observing is inferring hidden causes, and acting samples them",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "f142f38d-8b71-4b49-b7a2-96ce3392af64",
      "text": "Observation is inference: the brain never meets the causes of its signals directly and infers them. Actions such as eye movements are part of observing, since they sample the world to test predictions.",
